- Phase 2 verification after the metadata-support extension and AppTest recheck: 65 Pytest tests passed, including six focused AppTest cases and one complete supported-flow test for home render, image upload, invalid input, metadata sections, GPS reveal/clear, upload removal, and comparison. pip check and git diff check passed; local Streamlit health and page endpoints returned 200. The previous AppTest timeout did not reproduce, so its cause remains unknown; Arrow emits non-fatal sysctl permission warnings in this environment. AppTest can confirm the four tabs and their content render but cannot select a tab; actual browser tab switching remains unverified. No packages were installed.
- Phase 2 limits: GPS is not included in normal inspection results. XMP supports JPEG APP1, PNG `XML:com.adobe.xmp` text chunks, WebP `XMP ` RIFF chunks, and TIFF tag 700; IPTC supports JPEG Photoshop APP13 `8BIM` 0x0404 and TIFF tag 33723. JPEG Extended XMP is detected but not reassembled; when a standard packet is also present, only its parsed fields are returned with a limitation note. Other storage locations/formats are not parsed. XMP packets with DTD/entity declarations are rejected. Pixel similarity is a bounded descriptive mean-absolute-difference indicator, not SSIM or an authenticity score.
- Phase 3.1 is complete on develop: core/ela.py provides bounded JPEG-only recompression residual analysis; app.py exposes opt-in quality/scale controls and a side-by-side original/residual view. Latest verification: 16 focused ELA tests, eight AppTest interaction tests, and 82 tests in the full suite passed. No new dependencies were added.
- Phase 3.2 is complete: core/histogram.py provides validated, chunked RGB intensity counts across every frame; app.py exposes an opt-in pooled RGB distribution and labeled monochrome channel charts. The prior full-suite result was 91 passed after the multi-page TIFF correction. Follow-up verification: 8 histogram tests, 10 AppTest interaction tests (including clearing an upload after histogram calculation), and 92 tests in the latest full suite passed. `pip check` and `git diff --check` passed. No dependencies were added. Browser-rendered chart appearance was not verified through AppTest.
